/// DERIVED from real data, in GBP thousands: my own allocation of the pool by payroll full-time equivalent, one row per rule, financial year and participating department (the weighted many-to-many bridge between the pool and Department (current structure)). The weight is the department's average monthly payroll full-time equivalent in the year over the sum of the participants'; the allocated amount is the pool times the weight, rounded to four decimals, with the rounding remainder on the row of the largest weight (flagged in Rounding Row and stored in the rounding adjustment) so that the allocated amounts add up to the pool exactly. Only departments that publish workforce files, with at least the rule's minimum months in the year, take part. The annualised paybill is the average monthly paybill of the valid cells times 12. The full-time equivalent and paybill are real; the allocation is not a government figure and no real total adds it. The year's pool, and the total allocated in the year, are stored on every row (denormalised, labelled), so a user reads the pool only through the departments the user can see: there is no separate pool table, and a user with no participating department sees nothing of the allocation. A user who sees any participant can derive the pool from the weight and the allocated amount. The department filters it, so both security roles see only their own departments' rows. Source view dw.v_model_allocation_bridge.
table 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'
	lineageTag: a25658ca-8c94-42d1-a855-7939448b1501

	/// The pool of the year in context, GBP thousands: the real outturn of the Cabinet Office in the administration budget of departmental expenditure limits, read from the pool stored on the bridge rows in context, once for each year and rule. It is BLANK when no bridge row is visible, so a user who sees no participating department sees no pool; a user who sees any participant can derive the pool from the weight and the allocated amount. It is not changed by which departments of a year are in context.
	measure 'Allocation Pool' =
			SUMX (
			    SUMMARIZE ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)', 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Fiscal Year Key], 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Rule Key] ),
			    CALCULATE ( MAX ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Pool Amount (stored)] ) )
			)
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 6de24b53-58c2-44da-b801-6070872dfcea

	/// The pool allocated to the departments in context, GBP thousands: the sum of the stored allocated amounts (the pool times the weight, rounded, with the remainder on the largest weight). One pass over the bridge. It returns the same figures as the plain form kept hidden as Allocated Amount (naive) to within the rounding of the stored weight; docs/performance.md says what the rewrite changed and what it did not. Never added to Outturn.
	measure 'Allocated Amount' = SUM ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Allocated Amount (stored)] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 30f4e94d-d6ef-4a17-9469-50488e5fd906

	/// Kept as evidence, hidden, not for reports: the plain form of Allocated Amount (a SUMX over each department, year and rule of the bridge with a nested CALCULATE for the pool and another for the weight) that docs/performance.md timed and traced before the rewrite. For each department it multiplies the year's pool by the stored weight, and the engine holds each product to four decimals (a product with a fixed-decimal amount), with no remainder put on the largest weight; so it differs from the rewrite by the rounding of the products, at most GBP 0.40 (0.0004 in GBP thousands) in a year in the results (tests 952 and 953). It reads only the rows of the departments the user can see, like the rewrite. It is only here so that the comparison can be rerun.
	measure 'Allocated Amount (naive)' =
			SUMX (
			    SUMMARIZE ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)', 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Department Key], 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Fiscal Year Key], 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Rule Key] ),
			    CALCULATE ( MAX ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Pool Amount (stored)] ) ) * CALCULATE ( SUM ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Weight (stored)] ) )
			)
		isHidden
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Performance\Naive
		lineageTag: f02ce303-f08a-4216-b4fb-502ab34bbe9f

		annotation BestPracticeAnalyzer_IgnoreRules = {"RuleIDs":["UNNECESSARY_MEASURES"]}

	/// The weight of the departments in context: their average monthly payroll full-time equivalent over the sum of the participants', for one financial year. The weights of all participants add to 1. BLANK unless exactly one financial year is in context (a weight summed over years has no meaning).
	measure 'Allocation Weight' =
			IF ( HASONEVALUE ( 'Fiscal Year'[Financial Year] ), SUM ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Weight (stored)] ) )
		formatString: 0.0%;-0.0%;0.0%
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 882b8d0f-b8e3-44fc-aa05-91d80168d4ed

	/// The rounding remainder, GBP thousands: what the row of the largest weight was moved by so that the allocated amounts add up to the pool exactly. It is shown, never hidden. Zero on every other row.
	measure 'Allocation Rounding Adjustment' = SUM ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Rounding Adjustment (stored)] )
		formatString: £#,##0.0000"k";-£#,##0.0000"k";£0.0000"k"
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: b8ec1151-ac43-480b-84ab-f41a8850248c

	/// Allocated less the pool, GBP thousands: zero when every participating department is in context. BLANK when a department selection or a security role narrows the departments (a part of the allocation would be compared with the whole pool): the measure checks that the allocation in context equals the stored total of the year's allocation (the same on every row of the year). (ISCROSSFILTERED on the department table does not see a security role, which I found with the first run of the role cases.)
	measure 'Allocation Gap to Pool' =
			VAR Pool = [Allocation Pool]
			VAR Allocated = [Allocated Amount]
			VAR AllAllocated =
			    SUMX (
			        SUMMARIZE ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)', 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Fiscal Year Key], 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Rule Key] ),
			        CALCULATE ( MAX ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Allocated Total (stored)] ) )
			    )
			RETURN
			    IF ( NOT ISBLANK ( Pool ) && Allocated = AllAllocated, Allocated - Pool )
		formatString: £#,##0.0000"k";-£#,##0.0000"k";£0.0000"k"
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 8ab414e0-945e-4c54-bbf3-b5f2b0363361

	/// Average monthly payroll full-time equivalent of the departments in context, for one financial year: the weight's numerator. BLANK unless exactly one financial year is in context.
	measure 'Allocation Average FTE' =
			IF ( HASONEVALUE ( 'Fiscal Year'[Financial Year] ), SUM ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Average FTE (stored)] ) )
		formatString: #,##0
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 58b54054-7aac-45c7-84e1-350f4e798837

	/// The annualised payroll paybill of the departments in context, GBP thousands: the average monthly paybill of the valid cells in the months present times 12. Real data; it is the paybill the what-if measures work on.
	measure 'Allocation Paybill (annualised)' = SUM ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Paybill Annualised (stored)] )
		formatString: £#,##0"k";-£#,##0"k";£0"k"
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 6c0301d9-3f6e-4fc5-af62-79aad2540845

	/// Number of departments the pool is allocated to in the context: those with a row in the bridge.
	measure 'Departments Allocated To' = DISTINCTCOUNT ( 'Allocation Bridge (derived)'[Department Key] )
		formatString: #,##0
		displayFolder: Allocation
		lineageTag: 992a5012-3db3-4f66-b601-086e96e07cc2

